jobs.smartrecruiters.com/hvivoserviceslt.description_excerpt:
About This Job
The Senior Research Nurse plays a key role in the provision of cost-effective nursing services for optimal study delivery. The post holder will act as clinical project lead from clinical start-up to close out, this role is responsible for providing support as study coordinator on trials, and as a line manager for Research Nurses.
This role provides mentoring and supervisory support to the clinical hSITE team, study support to project teams and to maintain a ward environment conducive to study delivery.
With other members of the senior clinical team, the Senior Research Nurse ensures that all staff work in accordance to evidence based nursing practice, maintaining high standards of care, and that all tasks are performed in accordance with current regulatory, ICH-GCP standards and requirements and hVIVO standard operating procedures and policies.
Skills & Experience:
• Sound clinical knowledge
• Competence in the recording of vital signs
• Knowledge of Good Clinical Practice/Previous experience in a clinical trial setting
• Experience in phase 1 and 2 clinical trials
• Line manager to the Research Nurses;
• Study Coordinator;
• Assist with and oversee the daily management and allocation of workload within the clinical environment;
• Preparing, planning and execution of daily clinical activities;
• Provide guidance and mentoring to staff in the clinical environment;
• Ensure competence in performing their own and team’s daily tasks;
• Supervision and training of new ancillary staff in the clinical environment as required;
• Create or review and complete study related documents e.g. SOPs, logs, source data and CRF’s

About This Job
Overview:HVIVO is pioneering a human-based clinical trial platform to accelerate drug and vaccine development in respiratory and infectious diseases, specialising in early phase studies. Leveraging human disease models in flu, RSV, HRV and respiratory indications, the hVIVO platform captures disease in motion, illuminating the entire disease life cycle from healthy to sick and back to health. Our vision remains to become the partner of choice for companies developing products in airways disease that are seeking to gain early proof of concept around the effectiveness of their products and identify the ideal patient profile for later stage clinical development.
This is an exciting opportunity for a Research Nurse to join our team at our London site in Whitechapel, East London. As a Research Nurse you will support the Clinical Trial Centre with, day to day planning and execution of a clinical study, through screening and Quarantine. Experience working in First in human or Early stage studies required. Ideally with human challenge models experience.
Skills & Experience:
• Nursing qualification essential
• Research experience in Early Phase studies
• NMC registration essential
• Certificate in intermediate life support essential
• Competence in the recording of medical history, vital signs, ECG, phlebotomy etc essential
• Knowledge of GCP and previous experience in a clinical trials setting essential
• Good patient communication skills essential
• Previous experience managing the workload of a nursing team desirable
Main Responsibilities:
To maintain and promote the safety and wellbeing of all subjects participating in a clinical trial within the regulatory frameworks of ICH GCP, other statutory instruments and NMC Code of Conduct.
• Support Clinical Support Specialists in performing clinical assessments as per protocol;
• Perform nurse specific procedures as identified within the protocol;
• Performs informed consent procedures as identified in the study protocol;
• Completion of study related documents e.g. logs, source data and CRFs;
• Adhere to Company SOPs, protocols and Health and Safety Regulations;
• Use of expertise to input into the development of SOPS and other procedural documents;
• Maintain subject safety at all times responding to emergencies as per internal SOP and national guidelines and protocols;
• Monitoring and identification of the deteriorating subject, with appropriate escalation;
• Responsible for the checking of emergency resuscitation equipment as per SOP/OIs;
• Responsible for maintenance of medicines management within the clinical department as per SOP/OI;
• Responsibility for the supervision of clinical staff in the screening unit as delegated by the Senior Research Nurse;
• Identification of areas for service improvement;
• Promotes a high standard of practice and care at all times;

jobs.smartrecruiters.com/somfygroup/7440.description_excerpt:
About This Job
As a member of our Technical Support team, you will help professional installers diagnose and resolve technical issues with BFT products. Your ability to ask the right questions, identify the cause of a fault and explain the next steps clearly will help customers complete their installations and keep systems operating reliably.
The role combines telephone support with practical work inspecting, testing and, where appropriate, repairing returned components. Reporting to the Technical Manager, you will join a team of six technical support colleagues across the UK, sharing knowledge and working closely with our sales and warehouse teams. You will also provide occasional support with packing orders during busy periods.
Responsibilities:
Technical advice and customer support
• Provide telephone support to professional installers, guiding them through installation, wiring, programming, commissioning and fault diagnosis;
• Develop detailed knowledge of BFT’s product range, including hydraulic and electromechanical motors, control panels, transmitters and safety accessories;
• Use structured questioning to distinguish between product faults, installation issues, incorrect settings and mechanical or electrical causes;
• Explain technical instructions clearly and patiently, adapting your approach to the installer’s knowledge and experience;
• Take ownership of enquiries, record advice and agreed actions accurately, and follow up or escalate unresolved issues to the Technical Manager.
Inspection, testing and repair
• Inspect and test returned motors, control panels and other components to establish whether a fault is present and identify its likely cause;
• Carry out repairs where appropriate, within your competence and BFT’s procedures, and verify operation before equipment is returned;
• Document test results, findings and repair work clearly to support customer communication and internal traceability;
• Follow safe working practices when handling electrical, mechanical and hydraulic equipment.
Teamwork and operational support
• Share technical knowledge and recurring fault findings with colleagues to improve the consistency and quality of customer support;
• Work with sales and warehouse colleagues to ensure customers receive accurate information and timely assistance;
• Help with order packing when additional warehouse support is required during busy periods.

Qualifications
• Sound knowledge of electrics, basic electronics and mechanical systems; practical competence is more important than formal qualifications;
• Ability to interpret wiring diagrams, technical manuals and product instructions;
• Practical ability to inspect, test and repair components using appropriate tools and test equipment safely;
• Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a methodical approach to fault diagnosis;
• Clear communication and questioning skills, with a calm, patient and professional telephone manner;
• Ability to guide installers through technical checks and recognise when further investigation or escalation is required;
• Good organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise tasks, work independently and follow through on commitments;
• Ability and motivation to learn, retain and apply technical product knowledge;
• Confidence using IT systems to access technical information and maintain accurate support records;
• A collaborative and adaptable approach; experience in access automation, electrical installation, maintenance or repair would be an advantage.

Additional Information
• An attractive and comprehensive benefits package, designed to support your wellbeing, work-life balance and professional development;
• A varied role where you help installers solve technical problems and carry out practical testing and repairs;
• Product training and support from experienced colleagues to help you build your knowledge and confidence;
• The trust to work independently, take ownership of customer enquiries and put your technical skills to use;
• A friendly team where colleagues share what they know and help each other when things get busy;
• Opportunities to learn and develop within BFT Automation, part of SomfyGroup.
De bescherming van de persoonsgegevens van onze kandidaten is een verbintenis van Somfy. Daarom vragen wij elke kandidaat zijn sollicitatie uitsluitend via ons beveiligde systeem in te dienen, en niet per e-mail of per post.

